      "writtenOn": "2024-01-05T14:05:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "See my comment above - this check assumes that both the RSMRST input and PCH_RSMRST output are both configured for either active low or active high operation.  They could be different.\n\nIf RSMRST is renamed to RSMRST_PWRGD, I think it better matches the PDG documentation.  \n\nFurthermore, the common logic should use these assumptions:\n   RSMRST_PWRGD asserted \u003d RSMRST power rails valid\n   PCH_RSMRST asserted \u003d reset signal is active (PCH/AP not allowed to boot)\n   \nThe logic becomes, if RSMRST_PWRGD is logically asserted, then the PCH_RSMRST signal should be logically de-asserted.\n\nIf RSMRST_PWRGD deasserts, then PCH_RSMRST should be asserted.",
